{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for persistent upward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 2-4 EUR in the short term (days 1-5) following a price drop, failing to capture the immediate downward momentum.",
    "Adjust for lag in mean reversion: The model assumes a slow, linear recovery toward a stable mean (approx. 76-78 EUR), but actual prices exhibit sharp, volatile swings (spikes up to 79.80 followed by drops to 67.34) that the model misses entirely.",
    "Incorporate sentiment-triggered volatility: When sentiment history shows a mix of 0.00 and 0.67/1.00 (indicating mixed or recovering sentiment), the model fails to predict the subsequent price spike; increase forecast volatility in these windows.",
    "Reduce long-horizon forecasts: The model projects a gradual rise over 30 days, whereas true outcomes show a secular decline to ~67 EUR; apply a downward trend correction of 0.5-1.0 EUR per day for horizons beyond 10 days.",
    "Overshoot correction after spikes: After a price spike (e.g., 79.80), the model underestimates the subsequent crash; apply a negative adjustment of 3-5 EUR for the 3-7 days following any 2-day price increase >1.5 EUR."
  ]
}
